docker/workflow.yml is stale for the image's python mode: it expects
PREPARED inputs (the antibody_HL.zip / complex_HL.zip heavy-light zips plus
antibody_clean.pdb / antigen_clean.pdb / complex_clean.pdb) that the 8-step
pdb_tools preparation generates (the notebook's "Preparing" sections, or the
CI python suite's steps 0-8). Neither the image CMD nor the raw inputs
committed in docker/ (antibody.pdb, antigen.pdb, complex.pdb,
antibody_actpass.txt) produce them, so MODE=python cannot run the committed
workflow.yml end-to-end as published.

This file opts biobb_wf_haddock out of the publish chain's docker e2e gate
(publish-ghcr.yaml, select job): the image still publishes on template
changes (common/docker/**), untested, like every other workflow without a
docker e2e.

Coverage is not lost: the jupyter flavour e2e (tests/jupyter/run_test.sh)
runs the FULL pipeline — the same preparation + docking + CAPRI evaluation +
contact map — inside the very same image, so the conda env the docker
flavour would validate is validated anyway.

To re-enable: publish a self-contained docker/workflow.yml (preparation
steps included — the only blocker is that no registered biobb tool creates
the heavy-light zip files) or ship the prepared inputs in docker/. Delete
this file once tests/docker/run_test.sh can pass.
